      "id": "0fe7328633ffc9cb9717",
      "title": "AI Operating System",
      "location": null,
      "url": "https://www.vastdata.com/platform/ai-os",
      "description": "The AI Operating System Most AI teams manage separate systems for storage, data ingestion, analytics, vector search, streaming, and AI runtime. The VAST AI OS pulls all of it into a single unified infrastructure layer. One platform: Simple. Reliable. Secure. Read the White Paper Watch the Overview Capabilities What the AI OS Can Do The VAST AI Operating System captures any data at any scale, enriches it into meaning the moment it lands, and activates it across a global grid of GPUs. The VAST AI OS powers the performance, simplicity, and flexibility needed to support the next generation of sovereign AI workloads, and gives us the confidence to scale fast and securely. With VAST, we’re enabling a GPUaaS platform that meets the exacting needs of government, research, and enterprise AI customers in South Korea. DK Lee Vice President, and Head of AI DC Lab, SK Telecom Performance Powering AI’s Most Demanding Production Environments Technology How the AI OS Works Every capability in the VAST AI OS runs on a single architecture: DASE (Disaggregated Shared-Everything). DASE separates compute from capacity so each can scale independently, and it gives every node access to the full global dataset. That's how the AI OS keeps adding capabilities — database, event streaming, vector search, agent orchestration — without compromise. DataStore Unified Storage Every workflow starts here. Enterprise data, whether block, file, or object, is written to the DataStore, a single exabyte-scale foundation that consolidates all of it without the tiering and silos that slow AI. Best data reduction. Get the most value out of every PB of capacity you deploy. Explore DataStore DataBase Transactional & Analytical Database Next, data is chunked, embedded, and stored as vectors in the DataBase, alongside structured tables and streaming data, so unstructured and structured data streams are instantly ready for query and similarity search. 20× faster analytical queries vs. Iceberg stacks. Explore DataBase DataEngine AI Pipeline Automation The DataEngine then acts on it, leveraging python functions and a built-in Kafka-compatible message bus, triggering agents the moment data changes to take actions directly against it, turning a passive store into an active platform. Lower TCO and faster TTV with integrated Kafka and pipeline orchestration tools. Explore DataEngine DataSpace Global Namespace This makes that data available to the GPUs that need it, wherever they sit, leveraging a federated global namespace that spans clusters, within or across data centers, on-prem or off, from edge to cloud. Real-time access to any data, anywhere. Explore DataSpace Integrations Native Integrations Across the AI Ecosystem VAST connects to the tools your teams already use through native APIs, open-source plugins, and validated integrations. No rip-and-replace. Deploy alongside your current infrastructure and expand at your own pace. See All Integrations Explore the VAST Possibilities Talk to a Solution Engineer Get in Touch Email Us Contact hello@vastdata.com for a 24-hour response. Call Us Speak with a team member today at 212-658-1753. Contact Us Get in touch with us, and we’ll respond promptly! Explore Platform AI Operating System DASE Architecture Gemini: Consumption Model Supported Platforms Data Platform Services VAST DataStore VAST DataSpace VAST DataBase VAST DataEngine Scale-Out Solutions Company About Customers Press Releases Partners Careers Contact Resources Resource Library Blog Events The VAST AI OS White Paper Help Center Cosmos User Community Training & Certification © VAST 2026. All rights reserved End User Agreement Terms of Service Terms of Use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Cookies Settings English",
